# A finished command's pane is there to be read: it says `[exited 0] —
# Enter closes`, and Shift+PageUp / Shift+Home are still its scrollback
# keys (ghostty, too, runs its keybindings before a closing key). Only
# Enter or Esc closes it; any other key is the app's.
#
# 300 lines, exit 0; Shift+PageUp scrolls, a letter does nothing, Enter
# closes.
command view.toggle_tree
ex term seq 1 300
wait 1200
expect screen contains "[exited 0] — Enter closes"
key shift+pageup
wait 300
expect pane "seq 1 300"
expect screen contains "250"
type "q"
expect pane "seq 1 300"
key enter
expect screen lacks "seq 1 300"
